{"title":"Career Roadmap · Risk Analyst","role":"Risk Analyst","summary":"A Risk Analyst identifies, assesses and quantifies risks that could affect people, infrastructure, organisations, communities or critical operations. With a B.Sc in Disaster Management, the strongest pathway is toward disaster risk, climate risk, environmental risk, emergency preparedness and resilience analysis.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc Disaster Management"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is a good interdisciplinary pathway, but the exact meaning of \"Risk Analyst\" varies by industry. A Disaster Management graduate is better aligned with Disaster Risk Analyst, Climate Risk Analyst, Resilience Analyst, Emergency Risk Analyst and Hazard/Risk Analyst than with highly quantitative banking or financial-risk roles."},{"type":"note","label":"Career positioning","text":"General corporate/financial Risk Analyst positions may prefer finance, economics, mathematics, statistics or engineering backgrounds. A Disaster Management graduate should build GIS + statistics + hazard modelling + data analytics to establish a clear risk-specialist profile."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Main Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2027"},{"text":"Student / Risk Intern"},{"text":"Disaster science, hazards, GIS, statistics"}],[{"text":"2027–2029"},{"text":"Risk Analyst / Risk Associate"},{"text":"Risk assessment, GIS, data analysis"}],[{"text":"2029–2032"},{"text":"Disaster / Climate Risk Analyst"},{"text":"Quantitative risk, vulnerability, resilience"}],[{"text":"2032–2036"},{"text":"Senior Risk Analyst / Risk Consultant"},{"text":"Advanced modelling and risk strategy"}],[{"text":"2036–2040"},{"text":"Risk Manager / Resilience Specialist"},{"text":"Enterprise, climate and disaster resilience"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Risk & Resilience Lead / Principal Consultant"},{"text":"Strategic risk, climate adaptation and resilience"}]]}]},{"heading":"What Does a Risk Analyst Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A risk analyst asks:"},{"type":"p","text":"What can go wrong?"},{"type":"p","text":"How likely is it?"},{"type":"p","text":"What would be the impact?"},{"type":"p","text":"Who or what is vulnerable?"},{"type":"p","text":"How can the risk be reduced?"},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hazard identification"},{"text":"Risk assessment"},{"text":"Vulnerability assessment"},{"text":"Exposure analysis"},{"text":"Risk mapping"},{"text":"Disaster scenario analysis"},{"text":"Climate-risk assessment"},{"text":"Emergency preparedness"},{"text":"Business continuity support"},{"text":"Resilience planning"},{"text":"Data analysis"},{"text":"GIS mapping"},{"text":"Risk reporting"},{"text":"Risk-register development"},{"text":"Mitigation planning"},{"text":"Stakeholder coordination"}]}]},{"heading":"Understanding Disaster Risk","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A useful conceptual framework is:"},{"type":"h","text":"Risk = Hazard × Exposure × Vulnerability"},{"type":"p","text":"For example:"},{"type":"h","text":"Flood Risk"},{"type":"p","text":"Hazard\n→ Heavy rainfall / river flooding"},{"type":"p","text":"Exposure\n→ Population + buildings + roads + businesses"},{"type":"p","text":"Vulnerability\n→ Weak infrastructure + low preparedness + poor drainage"},{"type":"p","text":"Risk\n→ Potential loss to people, assets and economic activity"},{"type":"p","text":"A good risk analyst learns to quantify and communicate each component."}]},{"heading":"Build Foundation During B.Sc","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Disaster & Environmental Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"h","text":"Disaster Science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Natural hazards"},{"text":"Human-induced hazards"},{"text":"Disaster management 